A TOML outline lists the keys before the first table, then every table header as written, in file order: dotted tables and repeated arrays of tables stay separate lines.
A scalar value prints after its key, cut after its first line or 40 characters; inline tables and arrays print only the key.
A comment directly above a table starts its line range; a table's trailing comment and blank lines don't end it.
== args
input/Cargo.toml
== file input/Cargo.toml
# Build settings for the demo crate.

edition = "2024"
description = "A very long description that goes on past the cut"
notes = """
two lines"""
features = ["a", "b"]
point = { x = 1, y = 2 }
# The package itself.
[package]
name = "demo"
# Unused for now.

[lints.rust]
unsafe_code = "forbid"
[lints.clippy]
all = "warn"

[[bin]]
name = "one"
[[bin]]
name = "two"
